# Response headers for every path served by the Worker's static assets.
#
# THESE LIVE HERE AND NOT IN THE DASHBOARD: a file in the tree can be diffed,
# guarded (section 104) and shipped in a release; a dashboard rule can be none
# of those — and Transform Rules WIN over these, so the wire is read after
# every deploy (RELEASING.md, "The wire checks"). HSTS and
# X-Content-Type-Options are set at the edge and deliberately not duplicated.
# Content-Security-Policy stays in index.html's <meta>: the guards bless its
# hash against the one inline script.
#
# The two responses worker.js constructs restate the /* set themselves;
# guard 133 holds them equal to this file.
#
# Cache policy: sw.js and / are no-cache (revalidate before use — sw.js is how
# a returning browser learns the app changed, and a non-SW visitor must
# revalidate the document or a bad deploy is sticky). The fonts are
# content-addressed by qa/font-subset.json and take a year, immutable. The
# icons, the manifest, the share card and the install screenshots take a
# day: a year is only honest behind a hashed filename, and an unstable
# favicon is a listed Google cause of non-appearance. The agent-facing files
# and security.txt are no-cache: an agent asks once and writes the answer
# down.
#
# The Link: lines sit under /, not /*: a canonical relation is a statement
# about a document, and _headers matches on path only, cumulatively, with no
# way to unset. describedby points at /llms.txt, the same file the Worker
# serves to a client whose Accept prefers text/markdown; Vary: Accept on /
# says so to any shared cache. The seven rel=preload lines are for Early
# Hints (4.9.2): with the zone toggle on, Cloudflare caches them from the
# document's response and answers the next request with a 103 carrying
# them, so the seven font fetches overlap the HTML transfer instead of
# waiting for the parser. They mirror the <head>'s own preloads exactly —
# guard 104 holds the two sets equal and the fonts directory to both — and
# they are unquoted (rel=preload) where the document relations are quoted:
# the 103 path is specified against the RFC 8288 token form. The worker's
# two built responses carry the three document relations only (guard 133):
# a hint to preload fonts makes no sense on a markdown body. Permissions-Policy denies what the app never
# uses; interest-cohort is not listed and section 104 refuses it by name.
#
# /nocturne/* is the paper (6.2.0), and it is the one path whose CSP is a
# header: the app's CSP is a <meta> with a blessed script hash; the paper's
# policy is default-deny, written once here for every page the build writes.
# Styles, images and fonts come from this origin and nothing else. Three
# scripts run: the paper's own theme.js (6.3.0) and paper.js (6.5.0), and
# Cloudflare Web Analytics' beacon (6.3.0), which reports to
# cloudflareinsights.com. The app has none of them. Guard 164 holds the rule
# exactly. Both /nocturne/* and /hww/* say no-cache (6.5.1): the pages are
# rebuilt in place and a reader should never be served a stale issue; guard
# 104 pins it.
#
# The history of every decision above is in NOTES-history.md
# ("Where the served and config files' histories went").

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

/
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/>; rel="canonical"
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"
  Link: </fonts/limelight-latin-400-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/big-shoulders-display-latin-700-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/ibm-plex-sans-latin-400-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/ibm-plex-sans-latin-600-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/ibm-plex-mono-latin-400-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/ibm-plex-mono-latin-600-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Link: </fonts/bodoni-moda-latin-700-normal.woff2>; rel=preload; as=font; crossorigin
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Vary: Accept

/nocturne/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The paper's documents (6.6.2). / does not match /nocturne/, so a paper page
# was the one HTML response that sent no Link relations. The three document
# relations / already sends sit here, on the documents only: /nocturne/* also
# covers the stylesheet, the scripts, the feed and the faces, and a link
# relation describes a document (the same reason they left /* in 3.7.1).
# The front's canonical is the front. An issue's pretty URL is one path
# segment; :issue is that segment, and the assets plane writes it into the
# header value once (a placeholder is referenced once). Each issue's
# canonical is its own URL. Sitemap and
# describedby name the same resources / already advertises. The seven font
# preloads stay under /: the paper's pages do not preload faces.
# 6.6.3: Vary: Accept, the same reason / carries it. The worker negotiates
# a markdown representation of these two document URLs, and the HTML answer
# is the other one. A cache that stores only the HTML will hand it to a
# client that asked for markdown unless both representations say they vary.
/nocturne/
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/nocturne/>; rel="canonical"
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"
  Vary: Accept

/nocturne/:issue/
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap"
  Link: <https://nightwatcher.life/nocturne/:issue/>; rel="canonical"
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"
  Vary: Accept

# /hww/* is the crew's page (6.5.0): unlisted, so noindex twice (here and in
# the page), and a default-deny policy that runs no script. Guard 170 holds
# the rule exactly.
/hww/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# /privacy/* is the privacy page (6.8.2). noindex, like the page's own meta,
# and no-cache: the copy moves with a release. No CSP header: the page's
# policy is the meta in the file, and a second one would sit beside it.
/privacy/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/auth.md
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/orders.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/.well-known/security.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/icon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon-16x16.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon-32x32.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon-48x48.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/mstile-144x144.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icon-192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icon-maskable-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/share.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/shot-narrow.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/shot-wide.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/manifest.json
